2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] To forward arguments in a shell script on macOS, use `"$@"`. This preserves each argument as a
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] separate word, including empty or quoted strings.
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] Example wrapper:
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] #!/bin/bash
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] # relaypushd
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] dir="$1"
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] shift
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] pushd "$dir" >/dev/null || exit 1
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] "$@"
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] status=$?
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] popd >/dev/null
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] exit $status
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] Usage:
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] relaypushd ~/relaydeno task relaypopd
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `"$@"` expands to every remaining argument, exactly as given.
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] - Use `*` or unquoted `@` only if you want word-splitting.
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `$#` gives the argument count.
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] If `relaypushd` should simply pass all arguments through to another command without consuming the
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] first one:
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] #!/bin/bash
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] some-other-command "$@"
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] If that doesn't match what you're trying to do, paste the current `relaypushd` file and the exact
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] error or behavior you want.
2026-06-23 14:06:48 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
